eakin was an Australian lawyer and politician from Victoria, a leader of the federation movement and the second prime minister of Australia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/alfred-dent"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/alfred-dent.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Alfred Dent</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Alfred Dent was a British merchant who, with Baron von Overbeck, obtained concessions in northern Borneo from the sultans of Brunei and Sulu in 1877 and 1878.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/alfred-dreyfus"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/alfred-dreyfus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Alfred Dreyfus</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Alfred Dreyfus was a French artillery officer from a Jewish Alsatian family.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/alfred-freyberg"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/alfred-freyberg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Alfred Freyberg</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Alfred Freyberg was a German Nazi lawyer who in 1932 became minister-president of the Free State of Anhalt, the first Nazi to head a German state government.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/alfred-i-prince-of-windisch-gratz"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/alfred-i-prince-of-windisch-gratz.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Alfred I, Prince of Windisch-Grätz</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Alfred, Prince of Windisch-Grätz, was an Austrian field marshal who led the counter-revolution of 1848.</span></a></li></ul>
